From 5aeaa29ef90c2877bc19c123c3889289ed3c509d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:12:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] LOCAL TEST ONLY: soc: apple: display gate: Add the T8122
 dcpext route to the J613 front port

The J613 device tree wires the dcpext only to the left-back USB-C port
(typec0: ATC0's DP PHY and crossbar, crossbar state 2 = dispext1,0, DPTX
target 0) and leaves ATC1's crossbar disabled. On the left-front port the
USB-C controller therefore finds no display mode switch: a DP alt mode
partner gets USB only, and the monitor stays dark.

When the gate enables the dcpext on J613, add a second route in the same
changeset, so that the device tree in the boot loader image does not have
to change:
 - typec-routes/route@1 (mode-switch, endpoint) and port@3 (endpoint) on
   the front connector, linked like route@0 and port@3 of the rear one;
 - ATC1's DP PHY and crossbar as "typec1" in the dcpext's phys and
   mux-controls, the same crossbar state as route 0 (one pipeline,
   dispext1,0, behind either ATC's crossbar), DPTX target 1 (the
   firmware's DFP index of atc1, as in the M1/M2 dcpext routes);
 - status "okay" on ATC1's crossbar, and apple,always-on on ATC1's common
   power state, as the device tree has for ATC0.

The nodes are found through the device tree (route@0's graph, the one
other connector whose SuperSpeed lanes go to an ATC PHY, the crossbar at
that PHY's base + 0x4c000 in the PHY's power domain) and checked first.
If anything does not match, or the device tree already describes another
route, the gate says why and enables the dcpext with the routes it has.

The dcpext has one DPTX link, so one external display at a time; a DP
partner on the other port gets USB only while the first one is in use.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
